senses.gloss:
uddālakavrata
(‘penance [prescribed by] उद्दालक’)
------------------------------------------
Any boy born in the family of a द्विज (the twice-born) is expected to undergo the उपनयन sacrament within the prescribed age-limit, which is 16 years for a ब्राह्मण, 22 years for a क्षत्त्रिय and 24 years for a वैश्य. If he fails to do so, he is branded as पतितसावित्रीक or vrātya. (‘Sāvitrī’ means the गायत्री मन्त्र.)
One of the expiations prescribed for such a person to become fit again for the उपनयन sacrament is the उद्दालक vrata. Since the sage उद्दालक-आरुणि prescribed it, it has been named after him.
A person who performs this vrata should subsist on the prescribed ड़ोओद् as follows:
for two months on barley gruel;
for one month on milk;
for half-a-month on आमिक्षा (whey);
for eight days on ghee;
for six days on alms got without begging;
for three days on water;
and a total fast for one day.
(vide Vasiṣṭhasmṛti 11.76-79)
See also PATITASĀVITRĪKA.
